  {
    
    "name": "Section 4",
    "tag": "section",
    "class": "gps-637820982480011904 gps gpsil",
    "settings": [{"type":"paragraph","content":"Section design by GemPages. [Click here to start design](https://admin.shopify.com/store/0ggrd6-bp/apps/gempages-cro/app/shopify/edit?pageType=GP_STATIC&editorId=637820982312043136&sectionId=637820982480011904)"},{"type":"select","label":"Section Preload","id":"section_preload","options":[{"label":"On","value":"true"},{"label":"Off","value":"false"},{"label":"Off Lazy Script","value":"off_lazy_script"}],"default":"false"},{"type":"text","label":"Checksum","id":"checksum"},{"type":"html","id":"ggx0uDm8uFq_text","label":"ggx0uDm8uFq_text","default":"<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:17pt;\"><strong>You Thought It Was Maybe Just Your Testosterone\"</strong></span>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggni_ggNjOE_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggni_ggNjOE_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_31_58_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggni_ggNjOE_srcSet_mobile_src","label":"ggni_ggNjOE_srcSet_mobile_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_31_58_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggPEaFNaoCO_text","label":"ggPEaFNaoCO_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">When men notice changes in their sex drive, testosterone is often one of the first things they think about.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And understandably so.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Testosterone plays an important role in male sexual desire.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Some men discover that their levels are low and work with a doctor to address it.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Others get tested and find something confusing.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Their testosterone is normal.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Yet their desire still isn't what it used to be.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">So what now?</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">They start searching for answers.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe it's their weight.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe it's stress.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe they need to exercise more.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe they just need to accept that they're getting older.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Some start looking at testosterone supplements.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Others try changing their diet, going back to the gym, or cutting out alcohol.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Those changes can be worthwhile.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But they don't explain every case.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And here's something important that often gets overlooked:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Low sexual desire and difficulty getting an erection aren't necessarily the same problem.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">A man can want sex and still have trouble maintaining an erection.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Another man can have normal erectile function but rarely feel interested in sex.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Understanding that distinction matters because the possible causes—and the appropriate ways to address them—can be different.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggHi3wpFftB_text","label":"ggHi3wpFftB_text","default":"<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:17pt;\"><strong>The Part of Men's Sexual Health That Gets Overlooked</strong></span>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggIbPLBveV0_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggIbPLBveV0_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_35_33_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggIbPLBveV0_srcSet_tablet_src","label":"ggIbPLBveV0_srcSet_tablet_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_31_58_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggIbPLBveV0_srcSet_mobile_src","label":"ggIbPLBveV0_srcSet_mobile_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_35_33_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"gg9-GQcvO3t_text","label":"gg9-GQcvO3t_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">&nbsp;Think about a typical day for a busy dad.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">You wake up to an alarm.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe you didn't sleep particularly well.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">You drink coffee and rush out the door.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">You spend the next eight or nine hours dealing with work.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Deadlines.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Traffic.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Phone calls.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Bills.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Then you come home.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The kids need attention.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Dinner needs to be made.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">There's always something else that needs doing.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And at the end of the day, you're supposed to suddenly switch from handling responsibilities to feeling relaxed, connected, and interested in intimacy.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But your body doesn't operate in separate compartments.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your sleep, stress levels, physical health, and emotional well-being can all influence how you feel.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And that includes your sex drive.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"gga4DhNRyOu_text","label":"gga4DhNRyOu_text","default":"<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:34px;\"><strong>&nbsp;Its not always a testosterone Problem</strong></span>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggW2hPha3-v_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggW2hPha3-v_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_42_50_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggW2hPha3-v_srcSet_tablet_src","label":"ggW2hPha3-v_srcSet_tablet_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_35_33_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggW2hPha3-v_srcSet_mobile_src","label":"ggW2hPha3-v_srcSet_mobile_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/ChatGPT_Image_Sep_17_2026_11_42_50_PM.png"},{"type":"html","id":"ggou9D0_ekv_text","label":"ggou9D0_ekv_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">&nbsp;Sexual function involves several interacting systems, including hormones, blood vessels, nerves, and psychological processes. Stress, certain medications, health conditions, and lifestyle factors can contribute to difficulties.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">That means two men experiencing the same symptom may have very different underlying causes.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">One might have low testosterone.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Another might be dealing with poor sleep.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Another might have a medication-related issue.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And another might be experiencing several contributing factors at once.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">The important question isn't simply:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">\"How do I increase my testosterone?\"</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">It's:</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">\"What's actually contributing to the change I'm experiencing?\"</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Because once you understand that, you can start making more informed decisions about what to do next.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggwhRrh74MR_text","label":"ggwhRrh74MR_text","default":"<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:17pt;\"><strong>Why More Coffee Isn't Always the Answer</strong></span>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggZAXLWyc0y_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"ggZAXLWyc0y_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/2_1f8c15b9-008f-4eb3-84de-6158d31e80b6.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"ggZAXLWyc0y_srcSet_mobile_src","label":"ggZAXLWyc0y_srcSet_mobile_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/2_1f8c15b9-008f-4eb3-84de-6158d31e80b6.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"ggB-HUfPqOn_text","label":"ggB-HUfPqOn_text","default":"<p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Here's where things get interesting.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Many busy men already have a morning routine.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Coffee.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe two cups.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Maybe three.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">It's how they get themselves moving.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And there's nothing inherently wrong with enjoying coffee.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Caffeine can improve alertness and help you feel more awake.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">But feeling awake and being well-rested aren't the same thing.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">If you're sleeping five hours a night, another cup of coffee doesn't replace the sleep you missed.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">If you're constantly stressed, caffeine doesn't resolve the source of that stress.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And if you're experiencing a persistent change in sexual desire, coffee alone isn't a treatment.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">For some people, consuming too much caffeine—especially later in the day—can also interfere with sleep.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">So instead of thinking about coffee as the answer to everything, it may be more useful to think about your entire daily routine.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your sleep.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your physical activity.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your nutrition.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Your stress.</span></p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">And the habits you repeat every morning.</span></p><p><span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:11pt;\">Because these are all parts of the bigger picture.</span></p>"},{"type":"html","id":"ggSBBdD8q1m_text","label":"ggSBBdD8q1m_text","default":"<span style=\"background-color:transparent;color:#000000;font-size:17pt;\"><strong>A Different Way to Think About Your Morning Coffee</strong></span>"},{"type":"html","id":"gg3wtO5KIss_srcSet_desktop_src","label":"gg3wtO5KIss_srcSet_desktop_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/11_Testosterone_Benefits_._1060x_151e8ccd-5a6c-423d-a9fc-44a001ab71b3.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"gg3wtO5KIss_srcSet_mobile_src","label":"gg3wtO5KIss_srcSet_mobile_src","default":"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0653/0908/1645/files/11_Testosterone_Benefits_._1060x_151e8ccd-5a6c-423d-a9fc-44a001ab71b3.webp"},{"type":"html","id":"gg_ACMJFaVA_text","label":"gg_ACMJFaVA_text","default":"<p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Tongkat Ali (400mg)</strong> — An herb that's been investigated in studies of male hormonal health.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Ashwagandha (600mg)</strong> — A botanical studied for its potential effects on stress-related outcomes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Black Maca (1000mg)</strong> — A traditional root studied for sexual desire and other wellness outcomes.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Shilajit (200mg)</strong> — A mineral-rich substance investigated in limited studies of male health.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Arabica Coffee (8000mg)</strong> — The base of the blend, providing natural caffeine for alertness and energy.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>L-Theanine (200mg)</strong> — An amino acid studied for promoting calm focus without the jitters that can come with caffeine alone.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>Cacao (2000mg)</strong> — A source of natural compounds studied for mood support and antioxidant properties.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p><strong>L-Citrulline (6000